  "snp2.2:13.4": "<i>Durannaya.</i> Notice that being indomitable, a “raw stench” in a discordant person, becomes a positive trait in the awakened. This sort of contrast provides the basis for the wordplay that the Sutta Nipāta occasionally uses to describe the awakened in a paradoxical way. See, for instance, the conclusion to <a href='https://suttacentral.net/snp4.13'>Sn 4:13</a>.",
